# Progressive Tensors — authorized signer fingerprints (out-of-band trust root)
#
# THIS FILE IS THE TRUST ROOT.  Its authority comes from the git history of
# github.com/malaiwah/progressive-tensors — not from any artifact repo.  A
# consumer pins a fingerprint from here (or from a commit they have already
# seen) and passes it to the tools with --trust-signer.  Never copy a key out
# of the same download you are trying to verify.  See ../TRUST.md.
#
# Format: one record per line, whitespace-separated
#   <fingerprint>  <key-id>  <status>  <added-utc>  <role>
#
# <fingerprint> is the ed25519 public key in lowercase hex (32 bytes, 64
# chars).  For ed25519 the public key is smaller than a SHA-256 digest, so
# the key IS its own fingerprint — there is nothing to hash.  It is the same
# string that appears as "keyid" in fq-attestation/1 lines and as
# "signer_pubkey" in fq-manifest/1.
#
# <status> is one of: active | retired | revoked
#   active   accepted for new artifacts and for verification
#   retired  no longer signs; signatures made before <retired-utc> stay valid
#   revoked  reject, including retroactively — treat every signature as unproven
#
# Adding or changing a line here is a reviewable commit.  Rotation and
# revocation happen the same way, so `git log -p keys/FINGERPRINTS` is the
# complete, timestamped history of who was ever allowed to sign.

